<Base title="About Jules — Web & Mobile Developer" path="/about/"><section class="page-heading"><p class="eyebrow">THE PERSON BEHIND THE WORK</p><h1>About Jules Pecaoco.</h1></section><section class="split"><img class="portrait" src={content.site.profileImage} alt="Jules Alfonz Pecaoco" width="389" height="500"/><div><h2>{content.site.aboutHeading}</h2>{content.site.aboutBio.split(/\n\n/).map(paragraph=><p>{paragraph}</p>)}<div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="/resume/">View my CV ↗</a><a class="button" href="/contact/">Start a conversation</a></div><motto>Sic Parvis Magna. A reminder to keep building, learning, and moving forward.</motto></div></section><section class="section"><p class="eyebrow">STARTING A PROJECT</p><h2>A useful conversation<br/>starts with the problem.</h2><div class="capabilities"><article><h3>01 · Understand</h3><p>Who will use it? What is difficult today? Share the workflow, constraints, and outcome you have in mind.</p></article><article><h3>02 · Define</h3><p>Discuss the features, data, interfaces, and integrations needed to make the solution useful.</p></article><article><h3>03 · Plan delivery</h3><p>Agree on priorities, review points, deployment needs, and handover expectations before starting.</p></article></div><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="/contact/">Tell me about your project ↗</a><a class="button" href="/resume/">Explore my background</a></div></section><section class="section"><h2>Questions about my work</h2><article><h3>Who is Jules Pecaoco?</h3><p>Jules Pecaoco is the public short name of Jules Alfonz Pecaoco, a web and mobile application developer based in Bacolod, Philippines.</p></article><article><h3>What do I build?</h3><p>I build web, mobile, and desktop applications for attendance, record management, education, and business workflows. <a href="/projects/">Explore the projects and their technology stacks.</a></p></article><article><h3>Where can you review my experience?</h3><p><a href="/resume/">Review my CV</a> for dated experience, qualifications, and skills. My project pages include implementation details and source links.</p></article><article><h3>How can you contact me?</h3><p><a href="/contact/">Contact me</a> about a role, application, or collaboration, or email <a href="mailto:jules.pecaoco.dev@gmail.com">jules.pecaoco.dev@gmail.com</a>.</p></article></section></Base>